
Version 3.50:
- minor changes and bugfixes (total 46);
- "zero" digit in friendly codes is now printed with a dot inside of it in
  order to eliminate confusion with "O" letter (idea: M.Arrowood);
- mine field friendly code and universal code (if exists) are shown in the
  mine field info screen;
- "mf" friendly codes are not changed by the Alt-R randomization;
- VPA now reads PHOST configuration file (PCONFIG.SRC) if it's present in the
  game directory. HCONFIG.INI and RACES.INI files are ignored and not
  autocreated by VPA in this case;
- VPA now automatically creates PCONFIG.SRC file in the game directory if
  there exists UTILn.DAT file and it contains a PHOST configuration record;
- PHOST file transmission method (UTILn.DAT record 34) is now supported;
- gravity usage in Distance Mode has been changed. Instead of Alt-Enter you
  now press "G" key to adjust the pointer to the edge of the planetary warp
  well (a planet should be selected for this to work). Waypoint is not set
  automatically by pressing "G", you should set it with Ctrl-Enter or
  Ctrl-Click. VPA makes difference between round and "square" warp wells
  in PHOST. Default warp well shape (if there is no PCONFIG.SRC file) is a
  circle with 3 LY radius (as in Host 3.20);
- if ship destination point is located in planet N gravity well, then the
  ship info screen reads: "Dest.: ÷Planet N" (idea: T.Voigt);
- VPA now reads TARGETn.EXT file (created by VPUNPACK if there is more than
  50 visible enemy targets);
- new command-line switch: /K - keyboard-only mode. Disables mouse usage
  even if you have one (idea: K.Surkov);
- cosmetic changes in VPA.MSG file to increase PHOST compatibility;
- VPA combat simulator now has sound (many players would like to hear it).
  Sound can be turned on/off with "O" key in the sim screen. All weapons have
  different "voices";
- base damage parameter added to combat simulator (idea: S.Tatishev);
- in combat simulator: "+" and "-" keys can be used during the battle
  animation to adjust combat speed (as well as "1".."9");
- T.Wisseman's "M.I.T." interface (extended missions) support added. VPA now
  reads "MIT"-compliant MISSION.INI file and allows extended mission setting;
- ship cargo transfer interface has been improved. Apart from moving cargo
  by 1, 10 or 100 kt chunks (Left/Right arrow keys, Ctrl-Left/Right,
  Alt-Left/Right respectively), you can now transfer all cargo of selected
  kind by pressing Shift-Left/Right keys. Also you can manually input the
  amount of cargo (VPUtil users would appreciate this <g>) by pressing Enter,
  then using the numeric keys and then pressing Enter again. A field for
  manual entry is underlined with yellow color, you can select it with
  Up/Down arrows and the Tab key. Let's call it "Move-Or-Type" or "M.O.T.
  interface" <g>;
- M.O.T. interface in planetary builds. Now when you press "M", "A" or "D"
  key, you enter Structure Build mode where you can build mines, factories and
  defense outposts by pressing Right arrow key (Ctrl, Alt and Shift modifiers
  are active for 10, 100 and maximum possible number of structures building
  respectively). Enter key is also available for direct quantity input.
  Projected mineral mining rate and population happiness change are displayed
  "on the fly". You can also scrap excessive structures if you built them
  during the same Structure Build session (Left arrow key, Ctrl, Alt and Shift
  are active). Use Up and Down arrows to switch between mine, factory and
  defense building modes. Press Esc key to exit Structure Build mode;
- M.O.T. interface in supply selling;
- M.O.T. interface in base defence increment;
- M.O.T. interface in torpedo/fighter building;
- M.O.T. interface in tax level setting;
- M.O.T. interface in tech level upgrading;
- "U" key in a ship control screen unloads all cargo from the ship to the
  planet orbitted by the ship;
- Alt-U key in a planet control screen unloads all own ships orbitting the
  planet;
- "L" key in a ship control screen loads the ship with minerals/supplies/mc
  to build fighters or torpedoes (if the build is possible). You can specify
  how many fighters/torpedoes to build using the M.O.T. interface;
- VPA now asks for player password if there exists one (they say someone
  feels secure with those passwords <g>);
- VPA now allows to change player password (Alt-P key). Unlike PLANETS.EXE,
  VPA will require the new password next time you run it;
- new command-line parameter: /PW:password. You can specify your password
  this way as well as by typing it in;
- no more PLANETS.EXE runs. At all. Registered players shouldn't delete it,
  however, because it contains the registration information;
- PHOST v2.12 "client" command support added (idea: A.Sterian);
- target ship for Tow mission is now selected from the list of ships at the
  same location as the towing ship (idea: A.Bezborodov);
- target ship for Intercept mission is now selected using mouse and the list
  of ships at chosen location (idea: A.Bezborodov);
- VPA now uses Cloak Fuel Burn parameter in fuel calculations;
- ETA and estimated fuel burn are shown in ship info screen (idea: D.Subbotin);
- estimated fuel burn for a ship changes "on the fly" during cargo transfers
  from/to the ship (idea: T.Voigt);
- ship component parameters are now displayed in the ship construction screen;
- ship cost calculator in the ship construction screen remains active when a
  ship is being built (idea: A.Mazhara);
- increased visible diamether of planets on the map for all map resolutions
  except the full map mode;
- default color of enemy starbases on the map has been changed to light red;
- Del key now deletes the currently selected marker only;
- 15 colors are available for setting map markers now (was 7);
- new marker type: circle with a radius (r-circle). It has no text, it has
  a radius instead, that can be changed by player ("R" key in the marker info
  screen). Nearest r-circle marker can be selected by Shift-Enter or
  Shift-Click (like all other circle objects);
- marker of any type can be "bound" to a ship (own or enemy) and will travel
  with that ship (idea: V.Stavsky). To bind a marker to a ship, select the
  ship and create a marker (Ins key);
- custom map size support. VPA now supports map sizes from 1000 to 4000 LY.
  Point (2000,2000) is assumed to be the center of the map. X and Y map
  dimensions are assumed to be equal. Custom map size (different from 2000 LY)
  should be specified in MAP.INI file in the game directory as a value of
  "Size" parameter. For example, write "Size=1000" in MAP.INI if you are
  playing on reduced map where all planets are situated in (1500,1500) -
  (2500,2500) region;
- wrapped map support! PWRAP and Sphere, popular Host add-ons, make ships
  moving out of the edge of the map to arrive at the opposite edge, thus
  simulating a thoroidal universe model. If you specify "Wrap=Yes" in MAP.INI
  file, VPA will change its display respectively;
- Priority Build Points (PBP) are now stored in VPA database and displayed in
  the score screen (idea: Ch.Olin). The respective field is available in the
  report generator ("PBP" field in "Scores" section);
- enhanced score display. Differences from the previous turn are shown in
  the score screen;
- exit from VPA is reassigned to Alt-X or Alt-F4. If there were any changes in
  game data or VPA database, exit confirmation is asked with options to save
  data changes ("Y" or Enter), drop changes ("N" or BkSp) or don't exit (Esc)
  (idea: M.Lanko);
- team play support implemented! VPA now reads not only the specified race's
  game data, but other races' data too if all RSTs were unpacked into the
  same directory. The player can also see player-to-player messages received
  by all team members and all VCRs for the whole team. Password-protected data
  is not read, however, to prevent 'teaming up' with players who don't want it,
  unless correct password is specified via /PW parameter. But there is an
  exception for host masters: in order to provide a convenient way of creating
  game reviews, VPA reads password-protected data too when running with
  directory containing host data files for the game;
- new command-line switch: /O. Prevents VPA from reading other players' data;
- flexible color setup implemented! Now you can assign any display colors to
  planets, starbases, ships and mine fields of any race or group of races.
  VPA.INI file contains 3 pre-defined color profiles - "Own", "Ally" and
  "Enemy" that are assigned by default to the player's race, races whose data
  files are located uprotected in the same directory, and all other races
  respectively. VPA automatically creates a file named VPACLRn.INI in the game
  directory. This file contains default color profile names for all races.
  Editing the .INI files, you can re-assign pre-defined color profiles as well
  as define and use your own color profiles;
- color text highlighting feature added to VPA message editor. Fragments of
  text between pairs of "/", "_" and "*" symbols are highlighted with different
  colors (idea: A.Bezborodov). Highlight colors are defined in VPA.INI;
- new VPA.INI option (Interface section): StickyMouse=On/Off (default is On).
  VPA's anti-random mouse movement system appears not suitable for Windows NT
  users because of some properties of the NT mouse driver. It can be turned
  off by specifying StickyMouse=Off;
- VPA is now aware of Ship Cloning on/off Host config setting as well as of
  customizable cloning cost rates in PHOST;
- wormholes are now plotted on the map! They are represented by red circles
  of the corresponding radii on the screen (the color is defined in VPA.INI).
  Detailed information on wormholes can be displayed using Shift-Enter or
  Shift-Click (the same way as for all circle-shaped objects);
- Shift-W key toggles wormholes' visibility on the screen;
- Left/Right arrows (Ctrl-Left/Right for keyboard-only players) in a mine
  field info screen cycle through all mine fields (idea: J.Graesser);
- Left/Right arrows (Ctrl-Left/Right for keyboard-only players) in an ion
  storm info screen cycle through all ion storms;
- Left/Right arrows (Ctrl-Left/Right for keyboard-only players) in a wormhole
  info screen cycle through all wormholes;
- "C" key now centers view around the current pointer location (idea: T.Voigt);
- new command-line parameter: /REP:frmfile,repfile. Forces VPA to generate a
  report file with the name specified by 'repfile' parameter using form file
  with the name specified by 'frmfile' parameter. Report generation takes
  place at startup before switching to graphics mode. May be useful in
  conjunction with /B switch (idea: H.-J.Gurt);
- VPA now saves its current display status before exit and restores it on
  startup;
- VPA now has more respect to multitask environments;
- several doc files have been written.


Versions 3.48-3.49:
- minor changes and bugfixes (total 23);
- VPA compiled in overlay model and now consists of VPA.EXE and VPA.OVR.
  This makes more memory available for game data;
- VPA database structure changed. Data operations sped up and simplified.
  Old format database can be converted to the new format using VPADB6.EXE.
  It is recommended that you run VPA with /M command-line switch one time
  just after you convert your old database with VPADB6.EXE in order to gather
  some information that was not used by old versions of VPA;
- database reading on startup has been accelerated;
- no more limitations on the number of turns that can be processed by VPA;
- no more /L and /Q command-line switches;
- VPA now can browse VPAn.DB files without the current turn .DAT files (in
  read-only mode, of course);
- VPA now can correctly show incomplete (partial) planet and ship data
  (supplied by PHOST, for example);
- new command-line switch: /B. Runs VPA in a "batch" mode, when it reads
  current turn data, updates the database and terminates without entering
  the interactive mode;
- VPA now looks for its config file VPA.INI in two places - the main Planets
  directory (where you place VPA.EXE) and the current game directory. Thus,
  you can specify non-standard parameters for a certain game (f.e., ship
  colors) and use other parameters from the main VPA.INI file;
- new message processing subroutine. VPA now can extract useful information
  from messages using special templates which are user-defined! Message
  templates are stored in the file named VPA.MSG;
- VPA now extracts useful information from all host messages, including
  exploration, sensor sweep, super spy, dark sense and many others!
- ship explosions, mine hits, distress calls, planet and ship captures and
  many other events are displayed on the map as coloured crosses, flags and
  other markers! Marker types and colours are defined in VPA.MSG;
- VPA now uses real game configuration parameters. It creates a file named
  HCONFIG.INI in the game directory, where all parameters used by VPA are
  stored in the plain text style. VPA extracts the game parameters from Host
  messages. Most common default parameter values are used until you receive
  a Host configuration message for the first time during the game. You can
  affect some VPA readings by editing the .INI file;
- Ion Storms are now plotted on the map! They are represented by circles of
  the corresponding radii on the screen. Harmless ion storms are plotted in
  green, moderate in yellow, and dangerous in red (idea: A.Bezborodov), all
  the colours are defined in VPA.INI. Also plotted are the heading and the
  track of an ion storm (the same way as for a ship). Detailed information
  can be displayed using Shift-Enter or Shift-Click (the same way as for a
  minefield);
- Shift-I key toggles ion storms' visibility on the screen;
- added a facility for setting colour markers on the map! Press Ins to put a
  marker at the current pointer position. Markers can be of 6 different
  shapes and 7 colours. Markers are stored in the VPA database and never get
  lost on exit from VPA. A text label can be placed next to any marker. Label
  text and alignment can be changed using "T" and "A" keys in the marker
  info screen. Press Del to erase all markers at the current pointer position;
- Shift-A key toggles markers' visibility on the screen;
- no more VCR.EXE calls! VPA now has its own combat engine!
  Features:
  - 100% VCR.EXE compatibility (even the bugs from VCR.EXE are here! <g>);
  - fast and groovy combat graphics;
  - ship-to-ship and ship-to-planet combat simulation;
  - customizable battle parameters;
  - real ships and planets from the current game can be used in the sim;
  - left and right side ships can be swapped (Tab key; watch the LeftWin
    Syndrome with supercarriers);
  - correct Host 3.2 compatible Fed Crew Bonus and Engine-Shield Bonus
    implementation ("F", "E" keys);
  - Anti-LeftWin support (if the left ship is a carrier and the right ship
    has 141+ tw shield power (with E-S Bonus), then the right ship has 60%
    chance of receiving additional 360 tw of shield; Host 3.20 or better);
  - combat playback speed can be adjusted in the combat simulator screen or
    right during the playback ("1".."9" keys);
  - single step mode during playback (press Spacebar to turn the single step
    mode on, Enter or Esc to turn it off);
  - battle results can be re-used in the next battle ("R" key; survived
    ships/planets only);
  - for statistics fans: you can simulate more than 100 battles in a row
    with the same pair of ships, and all the battles will be different;
  - INSTANT BATTLE RESULT! Combat animation can be disabled ("A" key), and
    the result will be displayed immediately;
  - last simulated battle can be re-viewed ("V" key);
- added a starbase shipbuilding facility! No more calculations on paper, no
  more part-by-part ship building. You can see what you can or cannot build
  and why, you can play with the ship configuration and then build it all at
  once (though, you can build parts using the "+" key). Starbase tech levels
  are upgraded automatically when necessary. Supplies are sold automatically
  when there is not enough credits. All Host 3.2 special ship abilities are
  shown on the screen;
- added a facility for buying torpedoes and fighters on starbases ("Y" key).
  There is nothing more left that could be done with PLANETS.EXE but couldn't
  with VPA!
- added a facility for buying torpedoes and fighters right in the ship control
  screen when the ship is at starbase ("Y" key). New torpedoes/fighters are
  loaded directly into the ship's cargo bay. Supplies are sold automatically
  when there is not enough credits;
- added an automatic PLANETS.EXE start one time per turn. You don't have to
  run PLANETS.EXE no more (but don't delete it!);
- VPA now detects shareware and registered versions of PLANETS.EXE and
  maintains the same starbase tech limitations;
- added a minefield size calculator (Shift-F9). You can specify type and
  quantity of torpedoes, and VPA will plot the resulting minefield on the map.
  If you press Shift-F9 in the ship control screen of a torpedo ship, VPA
  will use the actual ship's parameters by default. VPA is aware of 'mdN'
  friendly codes and Robotic 4X minelaying bonus;
- no more external message utility calls! VPA now has its own message editor!
  You can create new messages, then edit or delete them, save messages to
  text files, load messages from text files (any rectangular area of text can
  be selected in a file), forward messages to other players, reply other
  players' messages with quoting, crosspost messages to any number of players
  by choice. Also you can view visual combat recordings (VCR) in the message
  editor and use battle results in your messages;
- PVCR support added. Now you can view PHOST battles in the message editor.
  To do it, you have to copy PVCR.EXE (from PHOST distributive) to the main
  Planets directory (from where you run VPA) and also place PCONFIG.HST from
  the current PHOST game to the game directory;
- VPA now keeps all VCR records, outgoing messages (written by you) and some
  of the most precious incoming messages (including all inter-player e-mail)
  in the VPA database;
- while browsing messages, if the current message contains information about
  a certain object on the map, pressing "M" or Enter key will force VPA to
  switch back to the map mode and find the object (idea: A.Sessa).
  Conversely, pressing F3 in the object info screen will force VPA to switch
  to the message editor and show the corresponding message;
- while reading a message describing the outcome of a combat you can view
  the combat itself;
- VPA creates a tiny data file named VPAMSGn.DAT in the game directory.
  Don't delete it (at least until you delete other .DAT files there);
- VPA report form language (VRL) keyword prefix changed from '@' to '~' for
  compatibility with BBS software that uses '@' character for internal needs.
  Old .FRM files can be converted to the new format with FRMCNVT.EXE utility;
- mouse-driven auto-scrolling of the map is now configurable and can be
  turned off by setting AutoScroll=Off in VPA.INI (idea: M.Zeveke);
- if you use mouse then the arrow keys will act as Ctrl-arrows when in any
  object's information screen. You can change objects in the focus this way
  (idea: V.Naidenov). The distance mode is the only exception, the arrow
  keys will act as usual in this mode;
- if Lizard ships with beam weapons, fuel and 'Hiss!' mission are orbitting
  a planet, then VPA uses this fact when displaying the population happiness
  change on the planet (idea: S.Steblev);
- when building planetary structures: supplies are sold automatically when
  there is not enough credits;
- added a facility for inter-player data exchange via subspace messages!
  You can send or receive data regarding planets, mine fields and map markers.
  To send data to other player(s), choose the respective object on the map
  (its info screen will appear in the right part of the screen), press
  Shift-F3 and choose the addressee(s). VPA will accept other players data
  via incoming messages only from players that have 'AcceptDataN' parameter
  in VPADATn.INI (see below) set to 'Yes', and only if you don't have newer
  data on the same object (note that the data transmission via subspace
  messages takes 1 turn);
- VPA creates file named VPADATAn.INI in the current game directory. This
  file contains a set of settings for enabling/disabling VPA to accept data
  via incoming messages from other players. No data will be accepted without
  permission. 'AcceptDataN' parameter allows or disallows VPA to accept data
  from player N and can be set to either 'Yes' or 'No';
- new command line switch: /M. Forces VPA to re-analyse incoming messages.
  Usually VPA extracts useful data from incoming messages only when you run
  at with the current turn for the first time. Specifying the /M switch could
  be useful when you change your mind on accepting data from other player(s)
  or when you edit file VPA.MSG;
- no more 200 LY limitation on waypoints. Now you can set any ship's waypoint
  as far as 3000 LY away;
- ship cloning (Host 3.20 'cln' code) support added. From starbase control
  screen you can choose a ship for cloning ("C" key; only when you have alien
  designed ships; works for all races but Privateers and Crystals). Ship
  construction screen will appear containing detailed listing of all cloning
  expenses. If the cloning is possible and you confirm your intention to
  clone the ship, it receives the 'cln' code, all other your ships at the
  same starbase with the 'cln' code have their codes randomized, and the
  starbase tech levels are upgraded to match the cloned ship's tech levels;
- context-dependent interactive help system implemented. Press F1 at any
  screen for instructions. File VPA.HLP contains help data. Help file name
  is defined in VPA.INI;
- graphic resource file name (RESOURCE.PLN by default) is now defined in
  VPA.INI. You can use alternative picture sets by changing this name;
- Switch Race support! Now you can use VPA in games with mixed races, f.e.
  a game of 11 Feds, or 3 Lizards + 4 Robots + 4 Rebels, etc. Prototype races
  for all players are defined in RACES.INI file (created automatically by VPA
  in the game directory) in form "PlayerRaceN = R", where N is player number
  in the game and R is this player's real race. For instance, in a game of 11
  Feds you should set "PlayerRace1=1", ..., "PlayerRace11=1";
- partial support of PHOST alliance features. VPA now can extract allied
  planet, starbase and ship data from UTILn.DAT files (idea: M.Alginin);
- added a hot key (Alt-Enter) for setting ship waypoint to the edge of
  planetary warp well (idea: M.Arrowood).


Versions 3.44a-3.44c:
- minor changes and bugfixes (total 7);
- added hot-keys for changing friendly codes of all ships/planets, that
  have the same code as the currently selected one. New code can be
  specified by player (Ctrl-F) or generated randomly by VPA (Ctrl-R);
- Ctrl-Left/Right keys now can cycle through starbases;
- Ctrl-Left/Right keys now find previous/next object regardless of whether
  or not it is situated in the current map window;


Version 3.44:
- minor changes and bugfixes (total 14);
- VPA in now aware, that there's no more minimum 25 kt mineral extraction
  for Fed with 100+ mines;
- partial support for a team play implemented. You can rename file VPAn.DB
  (race n database) to VPAm.DB, and all the race n's data will be available
  for race m. Once run for race m, VPA will add race m's data to the database.
  Then you can rename the file to VPAr.DB and add race r's data, etc.
  After gathering all allied races data, you can copy the resulting database
  to VPAn.DB, VPAm.DB, ... and all the allies will have each other's data.
  The only restriction is that you can issue orders only for the race which
  specified at VPA's command line. Also this feature would be compatible with
  PHOST's team play mode without copying databases;
- mouse re-initialization routine (Shift-R) now restores the cross-shaped
  mouse pointer (for compatibility with some drivers and Windows 95);
- population happiness change indicator added to the planet control screen;
- the fact, that a ship has only 1 engine, is now highlighted in the ship's
  equipment list (idea: A.Bezborodov);
- you can cycle planets/ships by pressing Crtl-Left/Right keys. If a ship
  was locked onto, then previous/next ship will appear (by ID number),
  otherwise - previous/next planet. Only planets/ships that are situated in
  the current map window will appear (idea: G.Yaltchik);
- starbase building function implemented ("B" key). If a planet has enough
  minerals/money to build a starbase, "Build starbase" option appears on
  the planet's control screen;
- added a hot-key (Alt-R) for randomizing friendly codes on all planets,
  which have a code other than "ATT" or "NUK" (idea: P.Porai-Koshits);
- added a mouse-driven map scrolling. To shift map window, move mouse
  pointer to the screen edge (idea: Red Troll);
- if a planet/base/ship control screen is displayed, all minor mouse
  movement (also jitter effect) is ignored ("sticky mouse");
- VPA now has its own text config file VPA.INI. The progam looks for the
  config file in the game data directory (specified in the command line),
  then (if not found) - in the current directory. VPA.INI structure is
  similar to Windows INI files (sets of options grouped into sections).
  VPA.INI file in this package contains VPA's default configuration;
- players now can specify VPA screen colors by altering parameters in
  the [Colors] section of VPA.INI;


Version 3.43 - the first version with English docs.
